<title>BELGIUM: EU clears Titanium/Valinox welded tubes venture.</title>
<headline>EU clears Titanium/Valinox welded tubes venture.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Friday it had cleared the creation of a joint venture in the welded tubes market between Titanium Metals and Valinox, a subsidiary of French steel company Vallourec SA .</p>
<p>It said in a statement that although the operation would give the companies a high share in the supply of welded titanium tubes in the EU, it had concluded that they would face effective competition from AST and major Japanese companies including Nippon Steel and Sumitomo. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
